  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A man named Matthew Brown says that in 2024 he figured out a secret program called Immaculate Constellation, said to gather government records of unexplained flying objects, and that Luis Elizondo, a former Pentagon official who worked on such reports, was tied to it by name. Michels passes on what Brown told him, calling it \"maybe the weirdest, most interesting thing.\" He adds that Elizondo then testified alongside the journalist Michael Shellenberger and said he could neither confirm nor deny whether he had been let in on the program, a story that also touches the filmmaker Jeremy Corbell."
